{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And now.</b> My Former — HaShem formed me to reprove Israel until they return to HaShem." "<b>Not be gathered.</b> The root, which is with a vav as in the qeri, and like it הוא עשנו ולא אנחנו (Psalms 100:3) and its companions. The Gaon [Saadia] said לא יאסף means 'he shall not die,' for his practice is to interpret according to the qeri and according to the ketiv. The correct view is what I said, only that the written alef stands in place of the vav, as R. Judah the Grammarian, of blessed memory, explained."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:41.170130262Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}